From 3000468a3777fad7175060d1e10dfc6071279f77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 11:29:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Simplify the distributed prometheus code and tests without
 changing behavior

Fold the wrapper's declared shard-skip settings into the resolved target
instead of a second accessor and two std::tie sites; probe the replicas
by zipping shards with their addresses rather than indexing with a guard
no reachable cluster needs; use the cluster's local shard count for the
local-shard pre-check; drop an empty-block check the executor never
returns; write hasInstantSelector as one expression; give the handler one
helper for "grant before existence, then the table"; test the target by
its cluster name where the sibling path already does.

Tests share error_code, keyed_result and the instant/range endpoint
switch through prometheus_test_utils, the write tests build their batch
through one helper, and every comment and docstring the branch added is
at most two lines. Coverage is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016i1XnLC3KypZdaYYsfzqub
